      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research suggests that the relationship between punishment and recidivism is more complex than a simple cause-and-effect. Studies have shown that while harsher sentences may deter some individuals, they often have little to no impact on recidivism rates for those with underlying mental health issues, addiction, or other chronic problems. In fact, some studies indicate that longer sentences can even increase recidivism, as they may lead to further marginalization and disconnection from support systems.",
      "source": "target",
